{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534490-v5-homebrew-new-ctuku-bloodline","id":1534490,"title":"(V5 homebrew) New-ctuku Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-20T08:25:46-07:00","id":1534490,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5 homebrew) New-ctuku Bloodline","content":"This was born out of lore I created for my current chronicle, thought I'd share the work-in-progress for feedback.<br /> <br /> <b>Absimiliard's &quot;Forgiven&quot; (bloodline, Nosferatu-only)</b><br /> <br /> Times change, and so do plans. At least, that's what Nosferatu theorize about what can only be their progenitor's latest scheme to strike back at its hated clan...as well as their eternal Toreador rivals. Some time after the rise of the Second Inquisition, certain Nosferatu -- mercy embraces, those who had been oppressed as mortals, the simply lost and dispossessed -- found themselves once again suffering the same tortuous physical changes wrought by the Embrace. Only this time, they emerged restored to their mortal appearances, if not more beautiful than they had been in life.<br /> <br /> While these Nosferatu lack the physical deformities distinct to the main clan, they are however perpetually tormented and followed by vermin.<br /> <br /> The change has divided the Nosferatu bitterly, breaking the unity and sense of community unique to the Sewer Rats. Some Nosferatu believe the change to be an attempt by their Antediluvian to divide and conquer the clan, for the Nosferatu to destroy themselves opposed to being perpetually hunted by the mythical Nictuku. Others believe it to be a new play in the Eternal Struggle -- Nosferatu capable of interacting freely with mortals, and with other Kindred without their appearance immediately betraying their clan, have pathways to achieving power impossible to their deformed brethren. Cleopatras, however, almost universally despise these Nosferatu out of jealousy and fear.<br /> <br /> Only Nosferatu with the variant bane Infestation may purchase dots in this loresheet at character generation. If at any time after character generation a Nosferatu with Repulsiveness purchases dots in this loresheet, their bane changes to Infestation.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Cleopatra's Visage:</b> Gain the Looks (Beautiful) merit. Additionally, you may purchase the Looks (Stunning) merit for only a single additional merit point at character generation, or for three experience (instead of six) afterwards.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Gorgon's Trick: </b>If purchasing this merit at character generation, you may select Presence powers with Obfuscate dots. Afterwards, when purchasing a new level of Obfuscate with experience points, you may select a Presence power instead of an Obfuscate power. Selected Presence powers must be at a dot rating equal to or lower than the new Obfuscate rating, and you must meet power and Amalgam requisites, as usual. Presence powers purchased in this way use your Obfuscate rating to determine dice pools and bonuses, instead of Presence.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Flesh of Janus: </b>If you do not already have the Protean power of Vicissitude, take it at no cost -- you do not necessarily have the discipline power, but rather a special variant of your own. This power works like Vicissitude, except you may only use it to alter your own appearance (Using your Resolve + Obfuscate dice pool instead of Resolve + Protean). If you do have (or later acquire) Vicissitude, you automatically succeed when altering your own appearance and no longer need to roll. Additionally, you gain the Nuit Mode merit (and this merit functions for you regardless of Blood Potency).<br /> <br /> Still brainstorming for the levels 4 and 5 merits. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T12:11:41-07:00","id":1534501,"title":"","content":"I like it and seeing it causing more conflict in a clan that values unity because of shared deformity seeing that changed and upsetting the apple cart makes for good storytelling and I can see their anti looking in from where ever he resides enjoying the conflict as amusements is far an few for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-20T18:19:56-07:00","id":1534515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534490-v5-homebrew-new-ctuku-bloodline?p=1534501#post1534501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it and seeing it causing more conflict in a clan that values unity because of shared deformity seeing that changed and upsetting the apple cart makes for good storytelling and I can see their anti looking in from where ever he resides enjoying the conflict as amusements is far an few for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for context I wrote this specifically due to the themes and narrative of this chronicle I'm running, which is going to be exploring racial justice and late capitalism in a fairly no-holds-barred context as it develops. The whole thing came as a &quot;eureka&quot; moment when I was talking about the Nosferatu variant bane with one of my best friends who happened to be in my old gaming group, and how with it one could do the previously unthinkable -- make a siren Nosferatu. He made a joke about a foxy Cleopatra (he and I both love blaxploitation); off to the races it was.<br /> <br /> It boils down to one thing. Absimiliard is one of, if not the most, unrepentantly and unforgivably evil Antediluvians, and whatever shenanigans he's up to at any time closely parallel mortal anxieties in the collective unconscious. Cold War fears of Manchurian candidates and nuclear annihilation just don't cut it any more, but in the wake of social media, Me Too/Time's Up, and Black Lives Matter he did something worse: take up the cause of intersectional feminism.<br /> <br /> So suddenly, Nosferatu who had been parts of historically-oppressed groups as mortals got their old appearances back and more. They emerged more beautiful, some with the ability to control their appearances as only Tzimisce previously could, and others the ability to nick some Presence tricks without ever learning the discipline. In other words, everything the Nosferatu ever envied is just theirs for the taking -- even their &quot;bane&quot; is something they can weaponize within the remit of their own clan discipline of Animalism, albeit at greater difficulty.<br /> <br /> Flipping the script on race, power, and privilege in the especially Masquerade-sensitive V5 setting, on a clan with little privilege, the ability to gain and wield power in only unconventional ways, and which previously could not care less about race sets the stage nicely for the Nosferatu to simply fracture and destroy themselves. But the question is, who in this new balance will prove themselves the &quot;new&quot; Nictuku?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T00:09:12-07:00","id":1536941,"title":"","content":"I never liked the retcon that The Nictuku are supernaturally beautiful. It's just stupid. They should absolutely hideous, and inspire even worse Delirium than Garou. I'm talking insides on the outside, overwhelming stench, vermin ghouls living in their body cavities. The most repulsive, blind terror inducing entities you can imagine. Besides their progenitor, who should be absolute terror and repulsion personified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:02:50-07:00","id":1537010,"title":"","content":"I thought this was an idea that Theodrim had for the Nosferatu in his game and not actually something happening with the metaplot and that the only Nosferatu ancient that was spared disfigurements was Yima and he might be a member of the Nicktu as Caleberos fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}